{"Using retryCount: reminder.retryCount + 1 is a non-atomic read-modify-write that can lose increments under concurrent processing": 0.607414186000824, "The second OR branch { retryCount: { gt: 1 } } in the deleteMany query has no method filter, so it matches and deletes ALL WorkflowReminder records (EMAIL, WHATSAPP, SMS) with retryCount > 1, causing silent data loss of non-SMS reminders every time the SMS cron job runs": 0.991025984287262, "If Twilio scheduling is skipped because SMS sending is locked, twilioProvider.scheduleSMS returns undefined and scheduleSMSReminders increments retryCount as if scheduling failed, which can lead to reminders being deleted after two runs even though no scheduling attempt was made": 0.8597735166549683, "The catch block unconditionally calls prisma.workflowReminder.update, but if that update fails (e.g., row deleted concurrently), the error escapes the catch and can fail the whole cron run": 0.8546872138977051}